  <static seed="17">
    <statement><p>Find the derivative of <m>\frac{x-4}{x^2+2x-6}\text{.}</m></p>
<p><m>f'(x)=</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{x^{2}+2x-6-\left(x-4\right)\mathopen{}\left(2x+2\right)}{\left(x^{2}+2x-6\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Using the quotient rule,</p>
<p><me>\begin{aligned}
          \frac{d}{dx}\left(\frac{x-4}{x^2+2x-6}\right)
          \amp = \frac{(x^2+2x-6)
          -(x-4)(2x+2)}
          {(x^2+2x-6)^2}.
          \end{aligned}</me></p>
</solution>
